"""Offline page for the exact algebraic nine-qubit fifth-sector maximum."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json,hashlib
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
checks=json.loads((ROOT/'independent-verification.json').read_text())
assert checks['fullPolynomialIdentityVerified'] and checks['attainmentVerified'] and checks['realBranchAndPositiveNormalizationVerified']
assert checks['certificateSha256']==hashlib.sha256((ROOT/'sos-certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
p=json.loads((ROOT.parent/'algebraic-s5-n9/parametrization.json').read_text())
def tex(t):return '<div class="proof-equation" data-tex="'+escape(t,quote=True)+'" data-display="true"></div>'
def sec(id,title,s):return f'<section class="reference-section" id="{id}"><h2>{title}</h2>'+s+'</section>'
body='''<section class="intro"><div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Exact algebraic certificate · 3 November 2026</p><h1>Nine qubits:<br><em>the maximum of S₅</em></h1><p class="intro-description">A degree-eight sum-of-squares identity over a real quadratic number field proves the sharp bound for arbitrary complex symmetric states.</p></div><div class="intro-aside"><span class="section-number">9</span><p>Proved global maximum<br>Exact algebraic verification</p><a href="../../index.html#n=9&amp;k=5&amp;mode=max">Open catalogue entry ↗</a></div></section>'''
s='<p>For every normalized pure symmetric nine-qubit state,</p>'+tex(r'\boxed{S_5\le\mu:=\frac{130928+6832\sqrt{61}}{1461}.}')
s+='<p>The maximum is approximately 126.13800532908574. The analytical state below attains equality.</p>'
body+=sec('theorem','The sharp maximum',s)
s='<p>The exact maximizing representative is</p>'+tex(p['stateLatex'])
for formula in p['radicalDefinitionsLatex']:s+=tex(formula)
s+='<p>All other Dicke amplitudes vanish. The positive square-root branches specify the real state. The verifier proves that this branch has positive u and Q, and verifies attainment exactly in the algebraic extension generated by t and the square root of u. Collective rotations also attain the same maximum. A complete equality classification is not claimed.</p><p><a href="../algebraic-s5-n9/index.html">Radical reconstruction and coefficient details ↗</a></p>'
body+=sec('state','An explicit analytical maximizer',s)
s='<p>For arbitrary, possibly unnormalized Dicke coefficients, set</p>'+tex(r'c_r=\sqrt{\binom9r}\,x_r,\quad q=\sum_{r=0}^9\binom9r|x_r|^2,\quad P_5=q^2S_5(\psi/\sqrt q).')
s+='<p>The explicit data specify a finite polynomial identity:</p>'+tex(r'\boxed{q^2(\mu q^2-P_5)=\sum_{B=1}^{'+str(checks['positiveDefiniteGramBlocks'])+r'}\sum_{m=0}^{2L_B}\frac{\mathbf v_{B,m}^{\dagger}G_B\mathbf v_{B,m}}{\binom{2L_B}{m}}.}')
s+=r'<p>Every component of <span data-tex="\mathbf v_{B,m}(x,\bar x)"></span> is a quartic polynomial with coefficients in <span data-tex="\mathbb Q(\sqrt{61})"></span>. Each matrix <span data-tex="G_B"></span> is real, symmetric and positive definite at the positive square root of 61. Consequently the right-hand side is nonnegative. Dividing by <span data-tex="q^4&gt;0"></span> proves the universal bound, and the displayed representative makes it sharp.</p>'
s+=f'<p>An independent verifier checks all {checks["allMonomialsIncludingCancellations"]} monomial coefficients, including cancellations, against a direct density-matrix derivation. All {checks["positiveDefiniteGramBlocks"]} matrices pass exact leading-principal-minor tests. Their largest size is {checks["maxMatrixDimension"]}; LDL decomposition gives {checks["squaredForms"]} weighted absolute squares. These checks use no floating-point arithmetic.</p>'
s+='<p><a href="basis.json" download>Explicit quartic polynomial vectors ↓</a> · <a href="sos-certificate.json" download>Exact algebraic Gram matrices and scales ↓</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json" download>Full verification report ↓</a></p>'
s+=r'<details><summary>Exact field arithmetic and polynomial conventions</summary><p>A coefficient stored as a pair <code>[a,b]</code> means <span data-tex="a+b\sqrt{61}"></span>, with a and b rational. Positivity is decided exactly by rational signs and comparisons of <span data-tex="a^2"></span> and <span data-tex="61b^2"></span>. Variable indices 0–9 denote the binomial-scaled amplitudes; 10–19 denote their complex conjugates. Monomials are lists of four variable indices. Divide each polynomial channel by the corresponding rational <code>basisScales</code> factor before applying its matrix.</p><p>The verifier encodes monomials as base-nine exponent vectors. Because the maximum degree is eight, multiplication is exact integer addition without digit carries. A common denominator reduces the full identity check to two integer coefficient comparisons, one for each field component.</p></details>'
body+=sec('proof','An exact algebraic sum-of-squares proof',s)
s='<p>The sector polynomial is reconstructed from the unnormalized reduced density matrices:</p>'+tex(r'(\rho_t)_{ab}=\sqrt{\binom ta\binom tb}\sum_{j=0}^{9-t}\binom{9-t}{j}x_{a+j}\overline{x_{b+j}},')+tex(r'P_5=126\sum_{t=0}^5(-1)^{5-t}\binom5t2^t\operatorname{tr}(\rho_t^2).')
s+='<p>The full expansion treats the amplitudes and their conjugates as independent formal variables. This covers arbitrary complex states, independently of the symmetry or real coefficients of the attaining representative.</p>'
body+=sec('derivation','Independent density-matrix derivation',s)
s='<p>Download the proof directory and run:</p><pre class="precision">python3 verify_certificate.py</pre><p>The verifier uses only Python’s standard library. It checks the entire polynomial identity, exact matrix positivity, the selected real radical branch, positive normalization, and exact attainment. The coefficients are large, so verification is more demanding than for the rational cases.</p><p><a href="verify_certificate.py">Standalone verifier</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json">Verification results and input hashes</a> · <a href="build_basis.py">Optional exact basis generator (SymPy)</a></p><p>Numerical optimization and selected coefficient equations were used for discovery. The independent verifier expands every coefficient; discovery samples alone are not used as a proof. This is a computer-assisted algebraic proof.</p>'
body+=sec('verify','Reproduce every exact check',s)
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Nine-qubit S₅ maximum · Exact algebraic proof</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>.proof-equation{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.4rem 0}.precision{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:var(--panel,#f0f1eb);padding:1rem}details{margin:1.4rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}.research-page main{max-width:1100px}</style></head><body class="research-page"><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../../index.html#n=9&amp;k=5&amp;mode=max">← Sector-length catalogue</a><nav aria-label="Proof navigation"><a href="#theorem">Theorem</a><a href="#state">State</a><a href="#proof">Proof</a><a href="#verify">Verify</a></nav></header><main>'''+body+'''</main><footer class="site-footer"><p>Extremal symmetric states</p><a href="../index.html">All proofs and remaining gaps ↗</a></footer><script>document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]').forEach(el=>{el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==='true',throwOnError:false,trust:false})}));</script></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'index.html').write_text(html)
print('Built exact algebraic S5 proof page.')
